# The bot images build with the repository root as context (docker-compose.build.yml,
# publish-docker.yml) and copy whole workspaces (`COPY validator-cli ./validator-cli`), so
# anything matched here never reaches an image. Patterns match from the context root
# only, unlike .gitignore, hence the `**/` prefixes.

# Operator secrets: each bot's .env holds PRIVATE_KEY and keyed RPC URLs.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.dist

# A host relayer's lock files: one baked into an image would seed a fresh state volume, and its
# route would fail on every start (claimLock finds the lock). The tracked state/*.json checkpoints
# still ship: a fresh volume is seeded with them instead of rescanning from block 0.
relayer-cli/state/*.pid
relayer-cli/state/*.pid.lock

# Host installs and build output: the image installs and builds its own. A stale local
# contracts/typechain-types would otherwise skip the contracts build in the Dockerfiles.
**/node_modules
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz
contracts/artifacts
contracts/cache
contracts/typechain-types
**/coverage

.git
